# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Open Innings — mobile app environment (example)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
#   cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env.local
#
# ⚠️ Everything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the app bundle and is
# readable by anyone who installs it. Nothing secret belongs here — that is
# what the prefix means, not a warning about carelessness.
#
# ⚠️ This file only affects a **local Metro** build. EAS builds run in the
# cloud and cannot see it; they read the `env` block of the profile in
# eas.json. So a value set here reaches `expo start`, and a value needed by a
# built APK has to be in eas.json (or an EAS environment variable).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the API and the website live.
#
# Unset, the app resolves the Metro host and assumes the web app is on port
# 3000 of the same machine — which is what you want when running `pnpm dev`
# and `expo start` side by side. Set it to point a local build at production.
#
# The `preview` and `production` EAS profiles set this to https://openinnings.com.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://openinnings.com"

# RevenueCat's public SDK key.
#
# Without it `purchasesConfigured` is false, the SDK never configures, and the
# paywall shows "Purchases are not configured in this build yet" with the
# button disabled. That is the correct behaviour for a build with no store
# behind it, and it is also what ships today.
#
# Two different keys, and they must not be confused:
#
#   Test Store key (starts `test_`) — for development only. RevenueCat is
#   explicit: never submit an app to a store configured with one. Belongs in
#   .env.local, never in eas.json, which is committed.
#
#   Android key — the real one, for a build that takes real money. Belongs in
#   the `production` profile's env in eas.json.
#
# Never the *secret* API key. That one is server-side and has no business in
# an app bundle.
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=""

# Whether live AdMob units may load. Anything other than "live" serves Google's
# test units.
#
# Two conditions gate a live ad — this, and a release build — because a live
# unit loading on a developer's machine is invalid traffic, and AdMob suspends
# accounts for it. `lib/ads.test.ts` asserts both.
#
# The `production` profile sets this. Leave it unset locally.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADS_MODE="live"
